    "text": "To determine how many guitar strings Dave will need to replace, we can break down the problem into smaller steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of shows Dave performs in total.\n2. Determine the number of guitar strings he breaks per show.\n3. Multiply the total number of shows by the number of guitar strings broken per show to find the total number of guitar strings needed.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of shows.\nDave performs 6 shows a week for 12 weeks.\n\\[ 6 \\text{ shows/week} \\times 12 \\text{ weeks} = 72 \\text{ shows} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of guitar strings broken per show.\nDave breaks 2 guitar strings per show.\n\\[ 2 \\text{ strings/show} \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total number of guitar strings needed.\nMultiply the total number of shows by the number of guitar strings broken per show.\n\\[ 72 \\text{ shows} \\times 2 \\text{ strings/show} = 144 \\text{ strings} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of guitar strings Dave will need to replace is \\(\\boxed{144}\\).",
